  "text": "A new website is supposed to be exciting, but my septic client was nervous and they had a point. A septic company we work with is getting ready for a new website. They told me what worried them about the switch, so I walk them through every step we take on launch day. Most of those steps we actually learned the hard way. Launch day is when the leads can quietly disappear through a form that looks fine, but actually sends nowhere. A good looking site is the easy part, making sure every lead still reaches your job is the real work. If you're switching websites, ask your designer how they'll prove your form works on day one. If they don't have an answer, send me a message.",
